Line 3: This Mutual Release and Settlement Agreement (this \"**Agreement**\") is entered into as of May 20, 2024 (the \"**Effective Date**\"), by and among:
Line 25: **C.** PGV was formed for the purpose of acquiring, renovating, and operating The Palmetto Grand Resort & Spa, a 312-room luxury beachfront hotel and resort located at 650 Mandalay Avenue, Clearwater Beach, FL 33767 (the \"**Property**\"), which PGV acquired on August 1, 2017, for a purchase price of Eighty-Seven Million Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\$87,500,000), funded in part by a loan from Gulf Atlantic National Bank (\"**GANB**\") in the original principal amount of Sixty-One Million Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$61,250,000) (Loan No. CRE-2017-06284) (the \"**GANB Loan**\");
Line 31: **F.** In connection with its exercise of the call option, PCG retained Whitfield Realty Advisors LLC (\"**Whitfield**\") to prepare an independent appraisal of PGV\'s real property and operating assets, and Whitfield delivered an appraisal report dated February 15, 2023, concluding that the Fair Market Value of one hundred percent (100%) of PGV\'s real property and operating assets was One Hundred Eighteen Million Dollars (\$118,000,000) as of December 31, 2022;
Line 33: **G.** Based on the Whitfield appraisal and the applicable provisions of the Operating Agreement, PCG calculated the buyout price for MSH\'s thirty-five percent (35%) membership interest as Forty-One Million Three Hundred Thousand Dollars (\$41,300,000), comprising Twenty-Four Million Two Hundred Ninety Thousand Dollars (\$24,290,000) attributable to MSH\'s thirty-five percent (35%) equity share and Seventeen Million Ten Thousand Dollars (\$17,010,000) in accrued preferred return, and tendered that amount to MSH on March 1, 2023;
Line 35: **H.** MSH rejected PCG\'s tender on March 10, 2023, and independently retained Beacon Valuation Group Inc. (\"**Beacon**\") to prepare a competing appraisal of PGV\'s assets, and Beacon delivered an appraisal report dated March 5, 2023, concluding that the Fair Market Value of one hundred percent (100%) of PGV\'s assets was One Hundred Fifty-One Million Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\$151,500,000) as of December 31, 2022, and MSH asserted a buyout price demand of Seventy Million Dollars (\$70,000,000), inclusive of a claimed bad-faith penalty under Section 12.7 of the Operating Agreement;
Line 37: **I.** On March 20, 2023, MSH filed a Demand for Arbitration with JAMS (JAMS Ref. No. 1440032871), asserting claims against PCG for (i) bad-faith valuation under Section 12.7 of the Operating Agreement, (ii) breach of fiduciary duty by PCG in its capacity as Manager of PGV, and (iii) breach of Section 8.3 of the Operating Agreement regarding capital expenditure and deferred-maintenance obligations, including an alleged Eight Million Two Hundred Thousand Dollars (\$8,200,000) in deferred maintenance (the \"**Arbitration**\");
Line 39: **J.** On April 5, 2023, PCG filed its Response and Counterclaim in the Arbitration, denying all of MSH\'s claims and seeking declaratory relief that the Forty-One Million Three Hundred Thousand Dollar (\$41,300,000) buyout price constituted the proper Fair Market Value under Section 12.4 of the Operating Agreement and that PCG had complied with all of its obligations thereunder;
Line 43: **L.** Pursuant to Section 12.4(c) of the Operating Agreement, which provides for the retention of a neutral third appraiser in the event the Parties\' respective appraisals diverge by more than fifteen percent (15%), the Parties jointly retained Linden Park Advisory LLC (\"**Linden Park**\") as such neutral third appraiser, and Linden Park delivered a preliminary indication of value in the range of One Hundred Thirty Million Dollars (\$130,000,000) to One Hundred Thirty-Eight Million Dollars (\$138,000,000) for one hundred percent (100%) of PGV\'s assets as of December 31, 2022;
Line 51: **P.** Contemporaneously with the execution of this Agreement, the Parties are executing a Redemption Agreement dated May 20, 2024 (the \"**Redemption Agreement**\"), providing for PCG\'s purchase of MSH\'s entire thirty-five percent (35%) membership interest in PGV for a redemption price of Fifty-Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$52,850,000) (the \"**Redemption Price**\"), on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth therein; and
Line 55: **NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants, releases, and agreements contained herein, the payment of the Redemption Price pursuant to the Redemption Agreement, and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged by each of the Parties, the Parties agree as follows:
Line 69: > \(e\) \"**GANB Loan**\" means the loan from GANB to PGV in the original principal amount of \$61,250,000, evidenced by Loan No. CRE-2017-06284.
Line 83: > \(l\) \"**Redemption Price**\" means Fifty-Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$52,850,000), payable in accordance with the terms of the Redemption Agreement.
Line 99: > \(e\) References to \"dollars\" or \"\$\" are to United States dollars.
Line 127: > \(h\) The alleged breach of Section 8.3 of the Operating Agreement regarding capital expenditure and deferred-maintenance obligations, including the Eight Million Two Hundred Thousand Dollar (\$8,200,000) deferred-maintenance claim and all related allegations of mismanagement, deferred repairs, and failure to maintain the Property in accordance with brand standards;
Line 141: > \(a\) PCG\'s counterclaim for declaratory relief filed in the Arbitration on April 5, 2023, seeking a declaration that the Forty-One Million Three Hundred Thousand Dollar (\$41,300,000) buyout price constituted the proper Fair Market Value under Section 12.4 of the Operating Agreement;
Line 249: **Section 7.1 --- Confidentiality of Terms.** The terms and conditions of this Agreement, the Redemption Agreement, the Redemption Price of Fifty-Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$52,850,000), and all negotiations, discussions, and correspondence leading to the execution of this Agreement and the Redemption Agreement (collectively, the \"**Confidential Information**\") shall be maintained in strict confidence by each of the Parties and shall not be disclosed, published, or disseminated to any person or entity, except:
Line 267: **Section 8.1 --- Tax Treatment.** The Parties agree that the Redemption Price of Fifty-Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$52,850,000) shall be treated for federal and state income tax purposes as consideration paid for the redemption of MSH\'s thirty-five percent (35%) membership interest in PGV, in accordance with the applicable provisions of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended (the \"**Code**\"), including Sections 731, 736, 741, and 751 thereof, and the Treasury Regulations promulgated thereunder, as well as any applicable state or local tax laws. The Parties shall report the transactions contemplated by this Agreement and the Redemption Agreement on their respective federal, state, and local tax returns in a manner consistent with this Section 8.1, and no Party shall take any position on any tax return, amended return, or claim for refund that is inconsistent with such treatment unless required by a final determination (within the meaning of Section 1313 of the Code) or unless the other Parties consent in writing.
Line 323: **IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the Parties have executed this Mutual Release and Settlement Agreement as of the date first written above.
Line 425: 5\. This Stipulation of Dismissal is filed pursuant to the terms of the Mutual Release and Settlement Agreement dated May 20, 2024, by and among PCG, MSH, Dominic R. Pellegrino, Nathaniel Cordero, and Elena Cordero.

